# The build context for the two web images is the repository root, because
# they share infra/nginx/app.conf.template. Without this file that context is
# gigabytes -- three node_modules trees, a Windows virtualenv, and the whole
# git history -- and every build pays for it before the first instruction runs.
#
# The backend image builds from ./backend and reads backend/.dockerignore
# instead; this file does not apply to it.

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.venv/
**/.venv/

# Host build output. The image produces its own; copying a stale one in risks
# shipping a bundle nothing in the image can account for.
dist/
**/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
staticfiles/
**/staticfiles/

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Secrets and local state.
.env
**/.env

.git/
*.log
**/*.log
docs/

# Backend-specific. The virtualenv is built for Windows: every shebang and
# every compiled extension in it is wrong inside a Linux image, and the image
# builds its own anyway.
backend/.venv/
backend/media/
